WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.326
Pearl was born sometime around 1898, give or take a couple of years,

00:00:03.348 --> 00:00:03.994
In rural Texas.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:06.681
As the only child of first generation and German immigrants.

00:00:06.681 --> 00:00:09.306
She was raised on a farm with a strict Protestant upbringing.

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:12.366
Her parents prayed before every meal and disciplined Pearl harshly when she

00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:13.102
stepped out of line.

00:00:13.156 --> 00:00:15.034
This continued well into Pearl's adulthood.

00:00:15.082 --> 00:00:17.242
Pearl's childhood was presumably quite lonely.

00:00:17.306 --> 00:00:20.618
There's no mention of siblings, cousins or friends of any kind in Pearl's life.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:23.806
It seems her only friends are the farm animals and the alligator that

00:00:23.828 --> 00:00:24.602
lives in her swamp.

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:27.014
Pearl imagination was a refuge for her growing up.

00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:30.098
She imagined a life for herself outside the farm, and she became obsessed

00:00:30.114 --> 00:00:30.802
with that dream.

00:00:30.866 --> 00:00:32.594
There was also a darker side to Pearl.

00:00:32.642 --> 00:00:35.474
Her mother mentions terrible things that she'd seen her do in private,

00:00:35.522 --> 00:00:37.042
presumably to the farm animals.

00:00:37.106 --> 00:00:39.042
Pearl even admits to this herself.

00:00:39.186 --> 00:00:44.262
-[Pearl] First, it was only animals smaller than myself, nothing with feelings,

00:00:44.326 --> 00:00:45.751
-[Pearl] nothing that could hurt me back.

00:00:45.751 --> 00:00:49.066
In her teenage years, Pearl met a young farmhand named Howard who came

00:00:49.088 --> 00:00:51.974
from an affluent background and chose to work on Pearl's family farm.

00:00:52.022 --> 00:00:53.930
Pearl pursued him, and they fell in love.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.702
She hoped that Howard would take her off the farm and show her a better life.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:01:00.238
They got married in the mid 1910s and even tried to start a family.

00:01:00.324 --> 00:01:01.658
But Pearl miscarried.

00:01:01.754 --> 00:01:05.038
Shortly after, Howard was drafted to fight in World War I, which would have

00:01:05.044 --> 00:01:07.210
happened in 1917 or 1918.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.514
Once again, Pearl's dreams were put on hold and she was trapped at home

00:01:10.552 --> 00:01:11.182
with her parents.

00:01:11.246 --> 00:01:14.507
Pearl dreamed of a life outside the farm, but that dream was always

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.308
just out of reach.

00:01:15.384 --> 00:01:18.514
She imagined one life, but reality handed her the same one that she'd always known.

00:01:18.552 --> 00:01:22.086
This repeated heartbreak turned into rage and combined with her

00:01:22.108 --> 00:01:25.202
constant isolation from the rest of the world, led her to do horrible,

00:01:25.266 --> 00:01:26.246
horrible things.

00:01:26.348 --> 00:01:30.022
If you want to know why Pearl did the things she did and how her own actions

00:01:30.086 --> 00:01:34.186
kept her trapped on the farm until her death in 1979, stick around to the

00:01:34.208 --> 00:01:35.022
end of this video.

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:40.757
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:01:40.837 --> 00:01:42.122
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:42.256 --> 00:01:45.318
By this point, you may be wondering, what's with the tank top? 

00:01:45.344 --> 00:01:48.430
Where's the usual Horror History shirt and tie? You need to be dress coded, sir.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.435
Well, today I am wearing this to let you know about the all new 

00:01:51.435 --> 00:01:52.970
CZsWorld Metal Merch.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.982
It's that time of year for shows and festivals, so I put together a product line

00:01:56.036 --> 00:01:59.666
with everything you'll need tank tops, tees and even a hoodie to keep

00:01:59.688 --> 00:02:01.426
you warm during that last set of the night.

