Once it's gone, it's gone.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.190
Link in the description.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:12.066
Pearl is the antagonist of Ti West's 2022 film X and the villainous

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:14.754
protagonist of the prequel, appropriately titled Pearl.

00:02:14.802 --> 00:02:17.606
In 1918, the world at large had fallen on hard times.

00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:21.958
America joined World War I in 1917, and the very real flu pandemic took the

00:02:21.964 --> 00:02:24.598
lives of over 675,000 Americans.

00:02:24.694 --> 00:02:27.930
There were no laborers around to help with farm work on account of the war,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.982
and by this time, Pearl's father was infirm and paralyzed.

00:02:31.046 --> 00:02:34.406
All of the farm work and responsibilities to keep the family alive fell

00:02:34.438 --> 00:02:37.354
squarely on the shoulders of Pearl and her stern German mother.

00:02:37.402 --> 00:02:40.346
Pearl's life mostly consisted of tending to the animals, reading old letters

00:02:40.378 --> 00:02:43.930
from her husband, and taking care of and bathing in front of her dad.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.406
You know, normal stuff.

00:02:45.508 --> 00:02:48.338
One, a bright spot in her life was going to the picture shows.

00:02:48.424 --> 00:02:51.394
Movies were brand new in 1918, and Pearl loved them.

00:02:51.432 --> 00:02:54.946
She even named her animals after the silent movie stars Charlie Chaplin and

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:55.774
Mary Pickford.

00:02:55.822 --> 00:02:59.078
Pearl dreamed of becoming a star herself one day and became obsessed with

00:02:59.084 --> 00:02:59.590
this idea.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.978
But to fully understand how Pearl turned from a dreamer to a killer, we've

00:03:02.994 --> 00:03:05.830
got to take a closer look at her dreams and fantasy.

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:07.445
(Impact)

00:03:07.562 --> 00:03:09.893
♪ Eerie Music ♪

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.194
The first time we see Pearl, she's dressed up and doing her hair in a three

00:03:13.232 --> 00:03:14.246
sided vanity mirror.

00:03:14.278 --> 00:03:16.694
She closes her eyes and gets lost in her daydreams.

00:03:16.742 --> 00:03:19.814
The lights go out and a spotlight shines brightly on her as she dances

00:03:19.862 --> 00:03:21.462
center stage in her own imagination.

00:03:21.526 --> 00:03:22.182
It's magical.

00:03:22.246 --> 00:03:25.402
But like all of the good things in Pearl's life, it doesn't last long.

00:03:25.456 --> 00:03:28.586
Pearl's daydream is interrupted by her mother, who scolds her for wearing

00:03:28.618 --> 00:03:31.806
her old dress, causing Pearl to storm out of the house in overalls and head

00:03:31.828 --> 00:03:34.134
to the barn to feed and perform for the animals.

00:03:34.202 --> 00:03:35.742
They are Pearl's captive audience, literally. 

00:03:35.806 --> 00:03:41.330
-[Pearl] Y'all see me for who I really am... a star.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.498
The performance is ruined by a goose who wanders in and steals the spotlight. 

00:03:44.504 --> 00:03:47.966
This is the first time that we see another, darker side to Pearl.

00:03:47.998 --> 00:03:49.938
Her disdain is written all over her face.

00:03:50.024 --> 00:03:52.802
She stabs the goose with her pitchfork and feeds it to her alligator.

00:03:52.866 --> 00:03:55.734
Despite the fact that her mother knows about her violent tendencies,

00:03:55.772 --> 00:03:58.002
She never tries to intervene until it's too late.

00:03:58.066 --> 00:04:00.886
Since she's isolated from the rest of the world, she never faces any

00:04:00.908 --> 00:04:04.042
repercussions and never learns to deal with her problems in a healthy way.

00:04:04.096 --> 00:04:07.558
This problem would fester and only get worse the longer that she was stuck

00:04:07.574 --> 00:04:08.102
at the farm.

00:04:08.166 --> 00:04:11.214
Pearl rides her bike into town to buy her father's morphine at the low, low

00:04:11.252 --> 00:04:12.490
price of two bits.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.738
How much is two bits, you ask? Famously, it's the price of a shave and a haircut. 

00:04:15.754 --> 00:04:19.710
-[Judge Doom] Shave at a haircut.
-[Roger Rabbit] Two bits!

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:28.174
While today, 100 bits is the equivalent of $1.40 on Twitch, back then,

00:04:28.212 --> 00:04:29.226
Two bits was a slang term for 25 cents. 

00:04:29.258 --> 00:04:32.878
Pearl buys the medicine and uses the spare change to get into the

00:04:32.884 --> 00:04:34.202
picture house across the streets.

00:04:34.266 --> 00:04:35.282
That's the movie theater.

00:04:35.346 --> 00:04:38.406
She sees a war movie where a soldier gets his face melted off, not the type

00:04:38.428 --> 00:04:40.306
of thing you'd expect to see in a silent movie.

00:04:40.338 --> 00:04:43.334
And Pearl is sipping her father's morphine throughout the show, so it seems

00:04:43.372 --> 00:04:46.690
likely that this movie is at least partly a product of her imagination.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.430
On top of that, this movie and the next one feature sound.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.150
And movies, weren't screened with sound until 1923.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.014
This could be an oversight, but it could be an indication that Pearl is

00:04:55.052 --> 00:04:55.862
projecting a bit.

00:04:55.916 --> 00:04:57.282
See what I did there? Projecting?

00:04:57.346 --> 00:05:00.606
The next thing she sees is Palace Follies, a movie featuring chorus line of

00:05:00.628 --> 00:05:01.898
dancing girls enamored.

00:05:01.914 --> 00:05:04.606
She takes the program and heads to a back alley to look it over, where she

00:05:04.628 --> 00:05:07.038
first meets the projectionist, who flirts with her and gives her a cigarette.

00:05:07.044 --> 00:05:09.998
He even cuts out a frame of the film reel and gives it to her as

00:05:10.004 --> 00:05:10.650
a souvenir.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.486
They chat and the projectionist tells her to take pride in caring for her dad,

00:05:13.508 --> 00:05:16.222
but advises her not to forget to live her own life, too.

00:05:16.276 --> 00:05:19.246
He says all the things that Pearl has been dying to hear, and he leaves her

00:05:19.268 --> 00:05:21.530
an open invitation to knock on his door anytime.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.746
As she rides her bike home with images of the Palace Follies girls dancing

00:05:24.778 --> 00:05:27.798
in her head, a gust of wind carries her souvenir film splice into a cornfield.

00:05:27.804 --> 00:05:31.106
So she goes searching for it and stumbles upon the perfect outlet

00:05:31.138 --> 00:05:32.978
for her loneliness: a scarecrow.

00:05:33.074 --> 00:05:36.162
-[Pearl] May I have this dance?

00:05:36.226 --> 00:05:39.446
And they dance. Pearl's dangerously active imagination is showcased as she gets lost in romance.

00:05:39.468 --> 00:05:42.826
She kisses the scarecrow and pictures the projectionist's face on it.

00:05:42.848 --> 00:05:44.940
Her darker side slips out.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.350
-[Pearl] I'm married!

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.502
Then she humps it and steals its hat.

00:05:48.566 --> 00:05:51.834
Scarecrow, if you're watching this, I know you probably like that hat, but

00:05:51.872 --> 00:05:53.862
some people you sleep with just steal your clothes.

00:05:53.926 --> 00:05:56.034
Just be thankful she didn't steal your Blackhawks hoodie.

00:05:56.102 --> 00:05:59.322
Back home, her mother scolds her for being late and for wearing a dirty hat.

00:05:59.386 --> 00:06:02.526
She once again bathes in front of her dad, this time strangling him a bit

00:06:02.548 --> 00:06:04.890
just to see if he'll react, which, of course, he cannot.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.030
Then it's dinner time.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.406
After a stern prayer, Pearl's mom interrogates her over the $0.08 that she

00:06:09.428 --> 00:06:10.074
spent on the movie.

00:06:10.122 --> 00:06:12.766
To give you an idea of how much they were hurting financially, that's the

00:06:12.788 --> 00:06:15.286
equivalent of a dollar 72 in 2023.

00:06:15.428 --> 00:06:17.586
Pearl lies and says that she spent it on candy.

00:06:17.618 --> 00:06:20.646
So her mom takes away her dinner and explains that she won't allow Pearl to

00:06:20.668 --> 00:06:23.894
wander around in foolish fantasies and hide from her responsibilities any longer.

00:06:23.932 --> 00:06:26.226
Pearl goes up to her room and prays.

00:06:26.338 --> 00:06:32.106
-[Pearl] Please, Lord, make me the biggest star the world has ever known so that I

00:06:32.128 --> 00:06:36.551
-[Pearl] may get far, far away from this place. Amen.

00:06:36.551 --> 00:06:39.686
Pearl's desperation for stardom was turning into her only escape,

00:06:39.718 --> 00:06:43.200
which was bad news for anyone who tried to get in her way.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.770
(Impact)

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:51.686
♪ Synth Music ♪

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.906
The next morning, Pearl's cow milking is interrupted when she gets a visit

00:06:54.938 --> 00:06:58.206
from her well to do sister, Mitsy, who arrives in a fancy car wearing fox

00:06:58.238 --> 00:07:01.986
fur in a nice dress. Mitsy's mother gives Pearl's family a roasted pig which

00:07:02.008 --> 00:07:04.478
Pearl's mother refuses out of stubborn pride and leaves it

00:07:04.494 --> 00:07:05.310
On the front porch.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.722
Pearl and Mitsy talk a bit.

00:07:06.776 --> 00:07:08.870
Mitsy is the closest thing Pearl has to a friend.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.986
They relate to one another, but maybe not quite to the degree that Mitsy expects.

00:07:12.018 --> 00:07:17.094
-[Mitsy] All this isolation has been enough to make one mad, hasn't it?

00:07:17.132 --> 00:07:18.326
-[Pearl] It really has.

00:07:18.508 --> 00:07:22.114
While X and Pearl were set during the 1918 flu pandemic, they were released

00:07:22.162 --> 00:07:24.326
in 2022 during the COVID pandemic.

00:07:24.358 --> 00:07:27.258
And this scene highlights a parallel between each time period, showing how

00:07:27.264 --> 00:07:28.934
the rich and poor were both isolated.

00:07:28.982 --> 00:07:31.354
But what that means for each of them is very different.

00:07:31.472 --> 00:07:33.494
Then Mitsy drops a bombshell on Pearl.

00:07:33.542 --> 00:07:36.654
There's a dance audition coming up at her church for a Christmas chorus line

00:07:36.692 --> 00:07:37.690
that'll tour the south.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.378
Pearl views this as her big break and agrees to meet Mitsy.

00:07:40.394 --> 00:07:43.518
There she steals her mother's dress once again and daydreams of dancing on

00:07:43.524 --> 00:07:44.158
the big screen.

00:07:44.244 --> 00:07:47.482
Later that night she sneaks out to the picture house where Cleopatra,

00:07:47.546 --> 00:07:49.774
starring Theda Bara is listed on the marquee.

00:07:49.822 --> 00:07:51.618
We'll get back to that name in a little bit.

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:53.374
Pearl knocks on the projectionist door.

00:07:53.422 --> 00:07:55.854
They share a drink and he shows her a different kind of movie.

00:07:55.902 --> 00:07:56.734
A stag film.

00:07:56.782 --> 00:08:00.514
According to director Ti West, this is a real stag film from the 1910s

00:08:00.552 --> 00:08:03.110
called A Free Ride and it's believed to be the first ever.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.686
These types of films were illegal at the time, so they could only be

00:08:05.708 --> 00:08:06.562
screened in private.

00:08:06.626 --> 00:08:10.214
But Pearl is still fascinated by whatever she sees on the big screen and

00:08:10.252 --> 00:08:13.546
because she sees herself as a star, she eventually imagines herself in that

00:08:13.568 --> 00:08:15.690
role which would come into play later in her story.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.746
The projectionist asks Pearl why she doesn't just leave her situation and

00:08:18.768 --> 00:08:21.030
Pearl says that she can't while her parents are still alive.

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:23.066
And that's when the light bulb goes off.

00:08:23.168 --> 00:08:25.010
-[Pearl] If only they would just die.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:27.022
The following morning, Pearl gets right to work.

00:08:27.076 --> 00:08:29.962
She takes her dad out to the pier to take a closer look at the alligator,

00:08:30.026 --> 00:08:34.922
which, by the way, is named just like Theda Bara from Cleopatra.

00:08:34.986 --> 00:08:37.674
This moment with her father and the alligator marks a turn for Pearl.

00:08:37.722 --> 00:08:40.846
She knows what she wants and she recognizes that life on the farm is keeping

00:08:40.878 --> 00:08:42.014
her from achieving her dreams.

00:08:42.062 --> 00:08:44.194
And for the first time she's doing something about it.

00:08:44.232 --> 00:08:47.182
She pushes her dad to the edge of the pier and says her goodbyes.

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:51.158
-[Pearl] It'd be easier for me if I didn't feel like I was abandoning you.

00:08:51.324 --> 00:08:53.746
-[Pearl] You understand that? I love you, Daddy.

00:08:53.778 --> 00:08:55.158
-[Pearl] But this is no way to live.

00:08:55.244 --> 00:08:58.978
Once again, her mother interrupts Pearl's fun and probably Theda's lunch.

00:08:59.074 --> 00:09:03.100
-[Pearl] Why do you hate me, Mama? 
-[Pearl's Mom] I only want what's best.
-[Pearl] hen do I get what I want?

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:07.242
Whatever screws were loose in Pearl's head before

00:09:07.296 --> 00:09:08.842
are rattling around freely now.

00:09:08.896 --> 00:09:12.266
She becomes incensed and a little aimless she steals an alligator egg from

00:09:12.288 --> 00:09:13.894
Theda's nest and brings it to the barn.

00:09:13.942 --> 00:09:16.926
She melts down in front of Charlie and Mary, and in a fit of rage, she

00:09:16.948 --> 00:09:20.014
squeezes the egg and imagines her husband returning home from the war and exploding.

00:09:20.052 --> 00:09:23.114
At dinner, Pearl's mom confronts her with the Palace Follies program

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:26.094
and Pearl informs her that she's going to a dance audition the next day,

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:29.038
explaining that she needs to try out or she's gonna regret it for the

00:09:29.044 --> 00:09:29.870
rest of her life.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:32.746
This is when Pearl learns that her mother knows about some of the horrible

00:09:32.778 --> 00:09:35.638
things she does when she thinks nobody is watching, her mother says the

00:09:35.644 --> 00:09:40.098
thing that Pearl does not want to hear.

00:09:40.274 --> 00:09:42.998
-[Pearl's Mom] You are not well, Pearl! It’s only a matter of time before you hurt someone else!

00:09:43.084 --> 00:09:46.054
The wording implies that she's hurt someone before, but we don't know

00:09:46.092 --> 00:09:47.398
exactly who she's talking about.

00:09:47.484 --> 00:09:51.138
It could be an animal, her husband, or maybe she's the reason that her dad

00:09:51.154 --> 00:09:51.922
is paralyzed.

00:09:51.986 --> 00:09:55.274
Or maybe she's not referring to a physical hurt, but given her history, I

00:09:55.312 --> 00:09:56.666
somehow doubt that's the case.

00:09:56.768 --> 00:09:59.690
As far as we know, Pearl has only killed animals up to this point.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:02.478
Whatever the case, she's on the ropes here and her mother doesn't instill a

00:10:02.484 --> 00:10:03.242
lot of confidence.

00:10:03.306 --> 00:10:08.826
-[Pearl's Mom] But when you fail, and you will fail, I want you to remember what it feels

00:10:08.858 --> 00:10:14.654
-[Pearl's Mom] like, because that's how I feel every time I look at you.

00:10:14.772 --> 00:10:16.522
This causes Pearl to snap.

00:10:16.586 --> 00:10:19.614
She slaps her mother and the fight commences until eventually Pearl shoves

00:10:19.662 --> 00:10:22.546
her into a fireplace and drags her burnt body into the basement as her

00:10:22.568 --> 00:10:23.822
father looks on in horror.

00:10:23.886 --> 00:10:26.834
Pearl's violent outbursts are motivated by her desire to escape her situation.

00:10:26.872 --> 00:10:30.166
So to cope with this, she turns to a different kind of escape and

00:10:30.188 --> 00:10:31.218
heads to the movies.

00:10:31.314 --> 00:10:34.118
That night, she sleeps with the projectionist and dreams of dancing on the

00:10:34.124 --> 00:10:36.006
big screen and her mother's burnt face.

00:10:36.108 --> 00:10:39.174
The next morning, the morning of the audition, he gives her a ride home.

00:10:39.212 --> 00:10:42.706
And so begins the most awkward morning after of his short life, where he's

00:10:42.738 --> 00:10:45.674
invited past the maggot infested pig that is still sitting on the front

00:10:45.712 --> 00:10:48.806
porch to meet her horrified father, who is still sitting at the dinner table.

00:10:48.838 --> 00:10:52.026
Pearl drags the projectionist upstairs, where she kisses him and

00:10:52.048 --> 00:10:53.750
talks of running away together forever.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:57.038
The mood is further ruined by Pearl's mom moaning like a banshee in the basement,

00:10:57.044 --> 00:10:59.434
which the projectionist insists they investigate.

00:10:59.482 --> 00:11:02.010
So she tells him that it's just the dog locked up in the cellar.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:05.870
This works for the time being, but Pearl is not a great liar because later,

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:08.734
while introducing him to all of her animals in the barn,

00:11:08.782 --> 00:11:12.034
Aka her best audience, she instinctively tells him that she doesn't have a dog

00:11:12.072 --> 00:11:13.122
when he asks about it.

00:11:13.176 --> 00:11:16.466
This is when the projectionist understandably makes up an excuse to get the

00:11:16.488 --> 00:11:17.282
hell out of Dodge.

00:11:17.346 --> 00:11:20.646
When Pearl recognizes that he's lying she turns on him real quick.

00:11:20.748 --> 00:11:21.750
-[Pearl] You're lying.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:23.318
-[Projectionist] I'm not.

00:11:23.404 --> 00:11:24.646
-[Pearl] Yes, you are.

00:11:24.748 --> 00:11:27.554
-[Pearl] I know, cause I feel things very deeply.

00:11:27.682 --> 00:11:30.886
This is one of our first clues as to what might actually be going on with Pearl.

00:11:30.908 --> 00:11:33.942
It's pretty clear that she suffers from some kind of mental illness,

00:11:34.006 --> 00:11:35.402
and possibly more than one.

00:11:35.456 --> 00:11:38.726
But this line might indicate that Pearl has borderline personality disorder.

00:11:38.758 --> 00:11:42.086
Now, I'm not a psychologist, and even psychologists have trouble diagnosing

00:11:42.118 --> 00:11:45.914
BPD at times, but she does demonstrate symptoms like extreme anger,

00:11:45.962 --> 00:11:49.322
extreme emotional swings, from extreme closeness to extreme dislike.

00:11:49.386 --> 00:11:50.810
Basically, everything is extreme.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:54.094
Pair that with a distorted self image, impulsive behavior, and issues around

00:11:54.132 --> 00:11:57.286
abandonment, and it's likely that this diagnosis would apply to Pearl.

00:11:57.338 --> 00:12:00.574
-[Pearl] Why are you leaving me? What did you say? Why did you change?

00:12:00.622 --> 00:12:01.342
-[Projectionist] You're scaring me, Pearl.

00:12:01.406 --> 00:12:04.194
That's not to say that people with borderline personality disorder are

00:12:04.232 --> 00:12:07.614
murderers, but in Pearl's case, she definitely is, as the projectionist

00:12:07.662 --> 00:12:08.466
would soon find out.

00:12:08.488 --> 00:12:12.006
When a pitchfork goes through his chest, she screams at him, stating that

00:12:12.028 --> 00:12:15.058
nothing and nobody is going to keep her on the farm, and finishes by sending

00:12:15.074 --> 00:12:17.362
the pitchfork right through his face with a stump.

00:12:17.426 --> 00:12:20.418
After heading back inside to say her goodbyes and tie up any loose ends

00:12:20.434 --> 00:12:23.786
before her life as a church dancer begins, she bids her mother farewell and

00:12:23.808 --> 00:12:25.638
gives her a taste of her own medicine.

00:12:25.734 --> 00:12:28.060
-[Pearl] I want you to remember what it feels like,

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:33.770
-[Pearl] cause that's how I felt every time you looked at me.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.086
However, she takes a much different tone with her father, cleaning him up

00:12:37.108 --> 00:12:39.834
and thanking him for everything before smothering him with a pillow.

00:12:39.882 --> 00:12:43.086
She rolls the projectionist and his car into the swamp, Norman Bates style,

00:12:43.118 --> 00:12:44.542
and heads off to her big audition.

00:12:44.606 --> 00:12:46.820
With everything riding on her success.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.007
(Impact)

00:12:51.898 --> 00:12:55.841
♪ Synth Music ♪

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:59.174
At this point, with her bags packed and her family killed, pearl has bet

00:12:59.212 --> 00:13:00.562
everything on the dance audition.

00:13:00.626 --> 00:13:01.862
There is no plan B.

00:13:01.916 --> 00:13:03.842
She even lets this slip in front of Mitsy.

00:13:03.906 --> 00:13:05.240
-[Pearl] It has to be me.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.890
-[Mitsy] I don't think you meant to say that out loud, Pearl.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:14.010
-[Mitsy] Well, if it's not me, then I hope it's you. Right?

00:13:16.011 --> 00:13:16.890
-[Pearl] It has to be me.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:21.253
While Pearl is focused and deadly serious, almost like an athlete in a pregame ritual,

00:13:21.253 --> 00:13:23.846
Mitsy is nervous and begs Pearl to switch places with her.

00:13:23.888 --> 00:13:27.134
She obliges and Mitsy thanks her, telling her that she's a good friend.

00:13:27.252 --> 00:13:29.518
-[Pearl] Am I? 
-[Mitsy] Of course you are.

00:13:29.604 --> 00:13:32.151
-[Pearl] Sister in laws have to stick together, right? 

00:13:32.151 --> 00:13:35.893
This demonstrates again that Pearl feels things deeply, gets super attached,

00:13:35.893 --> 00:13:37.970
and is hyper aware of how people see her.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:41.266
She ultimately just wants to be loved and appreciated, something she never

00:13:41.288 --> 00:13:42.178
got from her mom.

00:13:42.264 --> 00:13:44.062
Pearl finally gets her moment to shine.

00:13:44.126 --> 00:13:46.962
She enters the church and takes center stage, for real this time.

00:13:47.016 --> 00:13:49.510
Once again, we first see things as they actually are.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:52.502
Pearl's not a bad dancer, but she's not professionally trained either.

00:13:52.556 --> 00:13:54.662
Then we see things how Pearl imagines them.

00:13:54.716 --> 00:13:57.946
There are backup dancers, explosions, fireworks and a huge round of applause. 

00:13:57.968 --> 00:14:00.310
Then it all disappears.

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:05.434
-[Judge] Thank you, but it's gonna be a no.

00:14:05.632 --> 00:14:08.010
-[Judge] We're looking for something different today.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:12.822
-[Judge] More All-American, younger and blonde.

00:14:12.966 --> 00:14:14.502
-[Judge] Someone with X factor.

00:14:14.566 --> 00:14:15.854
Pearls can't believe it.

00:14:15.892 --> 00:14:19.264
She explains that it's the best dancing she's ever done and it can't be so.

00:14:19.264 --> 00:14:22.426
In her delusion, she sees the judge delivering the bad news as her burnt

00:14:22.458 --> 00:14:24.522
up mother in a moment of I told you so.

00:14:24.596 --> 00:14:28.238
After an unhinged fit of weeping and wailing, uncontrollably, Mitsy finds

00:14:28.254 --> 00:14:31.170
her outside and takes her home, where she accepts defeat.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:34.523
-[PEARL] Mama was right, I’m never getting off this farm. 

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:37.794
She wonders aloud if there's something really wrong with her, stating that

00:14:37.832 --> 00:14:40.486
there's something missing in her that the rest of the world has.

00:14:40.588 --> 00:14:44.134
Mitsy, naively trying to be a good friend, finds out that Pearl never told

00:14:44.172 --> 00:14:47.266
Howard about this insecurity and suggests that Pearl pretend that she's Howard.

00:14:47.298 --> 00:14:50.614
As she explains everything. Mitsy would comes to regret this

00:14:50.652 --> 00:14:53.994
decision because what follows is a nearly seven minute long confession and

00:14:54.032 --> 00:14:57.066
maybe the clearest insight that we have into what is actually going on in

00:14:57.088 --> 00:14:57.722
Pearl's head.

00:14:57.776 --> 00:15:01.306
She confesses that she's angry at Howard, that she cheated on him, that she

00:15:01.328 --> 00:15:04.246
tried to use him as a way to get off the farm, that she didn't like being

00:15:04.288 --> 00:15:07.098
pregnant with Howard's baby, and that she's glad that the pregnancy didn't

00:15:07.114 --> 00:15:07.662
pan out.

00:15:07.716 --> 00:15:11.482
She envies his perfect life and laments how her prayers are never answered.

00:15:11.546 --> 00:15:14.366
She also expresses jealousy for the pretty girls in the movie.

00:15:14.478 --> 00:15:16.690
-[Pearl] I want what they have so badly.

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:18.260
-[Pearl] To be perfect.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:21.298
-[Pearl] To be loved from as many people as possible.

00:15:21.384 --> 00:15:26.146
-[Pearl] To make up for all my time spent suffering. Sometimes I wake in the middle of the

00:15:26.168 --> 00:15:27.906
-[Pearl] night and the fear washes over me.

00:15:27.928 --> 00:15:32.130
-[Pearl] Because what if this is it? What if this is right where I belong? Failure.

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.354
This is part of what gives Pearl depth as a villain.

00:15:34.402 --> 00:15:37.126
She's honest and she wants to be loved, just as all people do

00:15:37.148 --> 00:15:37.890
To some extent.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:42.114
She's full of normal human emotions like self pity, envy, regret and fear.

00:15:42.162 --> 00:15:45.162
But cranked up to eleven in terms of how fervently she feels them.

00:15:45.216 --> 00:15:48.394
Seemingly without realizing it, she moves on from things she shouldn't have

00:15:48.432 --> 00:15:50.726
said to things she really shouldn't have said.

00:15:50.848 --> 00:15:53.854
-[Pearl] I'm so scared that when you finally come home you'll see me and be

00:15:53.892 --> 00:15:55.790
-[Pearl] frightened like everyone else is.

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:57.520
-[Pearl] I know what I've done.

00:15:58.210 --> 00:15:59.360
-[Pearl] Bad things.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.310
-[Pearl] Terrible, awful, murderous things.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:07.042
She reveals everything, claiming that killing is easier than you'd think,

00:16:07.096 --> 00:16:10.274
then begs for forgiveness, promising to make things right and make a life

00:16:10.312 --> 00:16:11.182
for them on the farm.

00:16:11.246 --> 00:16:12.260
-[Pearl] It'd be enough.

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:15.438
Just you and me here on this farm.

00:16:15.534 --> 00:16:17.678
-[Pearl] All I really want is to be loved.

00:16:17.774 --> 00:16:20.062
-[Pearl] I'm having such a hard time without it lately.

00:16:20.126 --> 00:16:22.918
It's the first time that Pearl has ever expressed interest in staying on the

00:16:22.924 --> 00:16:24.754
farm, apparently giving up on her dreams.

00:16:24.802 --> 00:16:26.614
And judging by how her story plays out.

00:16:26.652 --> 00:16:29.766
She must have meant it, but her proclivity towards fame and beauty would

00:16:29.788 --> 00:16:31.046
stick with her over the years.

00:16:31.148 --> 00:16:34.346
Finally, for the first time in minutes, she looks up at her poor sister in law,

00:16:34.368 --> 00:16:36.214
who is absolutely shell shocked.

00:16:36.262 --> 00:16:39.306
Mitsy makes up an excuse to leave, just like the projectionist did a few

00:16:39.328 --> 00:16:42.838
hours earlier, and Pearl recognizes this immediately and asks Mitsy if she's

00:16:42.854 --> 00:16:43.514
frightened of her.

00:16:43.552 --> 00:16:46.414
Mitsy assures her that all is well, but Pearl doesn't buy it.

00:16:46.452 --> 00:16:49.562
But instead of calling Mitsy you on the lie, she takes it one step further.

00:16:49.626 --> 00:16:52.122
She congratulates her on getting the part in the dance troupe.

00:16:52.186 --> 00:16:55.326
Mitsy at first denies that she got the part, but Pearl insists that she

00:16:55.348 --> 00:16:58.798
doesn't need to lie until she relents and tells Pearl that she got the part.

00:16:58.884 --> 00:17:01.726
It's a little unclear if she actually did get the part, or if she is once

00:17:01.748 --> 00:17:04.638
again trying to tell Pearl what she wants to hear in order to escape the situation. 

00:17:04.644 --> 00:17:08.246
Whatever the case, one thing is clear pearl believes it and she

00:17:08.268 --> 00:17:10.920
doesn't like it, leading things to take a dark turn.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.650
– [Pearl] You always get everything you want.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:16.070
Pearl tries to assure Mitsy that she loves Howard and can fix things.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:19.862
She begs her not to tell anybody what she's done, to which Mitsy agrees, but

00:17:19.916 --> 00:17:23.622
not convincingly enough, Pearl chases her down and murders her with an axe.

00:17:23.686 --> 00:17:24.810
This one is different, though.

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:28.006
This time she's not motivated by someone getting in the way of her stardom

00:17:28.038 --> 00:17:31.030
or anger or rejection, but rather out of self preservation.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.934
She wants to keep what she's got with Howard, and Mitsy knows too much,

00:17:33.972 --> 00:17:35.866
thanks to their little role play exercise.

00:17:35.978 --> 00:17:38.990
-[Pearl] It's not about what I want anymore, Mitsy.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:42.366
-[Pearl] It's about making the best of what I have.

00:17:42.468 --> 00:17:45.806
Pearl returns to the basement and does her best to patch things up with her

00:17:45.828 --> 00:17:46.362
dead mother.

00:17:46.426 --> 00:17:49.934
She lays down and combs her hair, using her powerful imagination to daydream

00:17:49.982 --> 00:17:52.510
of a life where her mom loved her and sang her lullabies.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:56.114
She's falling into a state of complete disassociation from reality in order

00:17:56.152 --> 00:17:57.854
to continue thriving in her fantasy.

00:17:57.902 --> 00:18:01.362
She chops up Mitsy and feeds her to Theta, the luckiest gator on earth, probably, 

00:18:01.426 --> 00:18:05.186
then sets the table for a lovely maggot infested porched pig dinner

00:18:05.218 --> 00:18:06.386
with her parents' corpses.

00:18:06.498 --> 00:18:09.446
Her complete mental breakdown could not have come at a better time for her husband,

00:18:09.468 --> 00:18:12.762
who had just been discharged from the war and was on his way home

00:18:12.816 --> 00:18:14.262
to discover this horrific scene.

00:18:14.326 --> 00:18:18.006
When he arrives, Pearl does her best to play it cool, but fails miserably.

00:18:18.118 --> 00:18:18.890
-[Pearl] Howard,

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.486
-[Pearl] I'm so happy you're home.

00:18:24.608 --> 00:18:29.374
Pearl smiles at her husband and smiles and smiles and she cries a little and

00:18:29.412 --> 00:18:30.202
keeps smiling.

00:18:30.266 --> 00:18:33.146
Her loneliness after Howard went to fight in the war was the main catalyst

00:18:33.178 --> 00:18:36.494
that drove her over the edge, and his unexpected return essentially broke

00:18:36.542 --> 00:18:37.198
her brain.

00:18:37.294 --> 00:18:40.770
We don't know for sure what happened next, but we do know that, for whatever

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:45.700
reason, Howard stuck around for another 61 years!

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.250
(Impact)

00:18:50.854 --> 00:18:54.652
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:58.706
After Howard returns from the horrors of war only to discover that his wife

00:18:58.738 --> 00:19:02.278
has made a horrifying scene of their own home, he presumably helps her hide

00:19:02.294 --> 00:19:02.902
the evidence.

00:19:02.966 --> 00:19:05.722
And given that they lived in the countryside, it's unlikely that anyone

00:19:05.776 --> 00:19:06.998
would have come investigating.

00:19:07.094 --> 00:19:10.486
It's possible that he just enjoyed working on the farm and felt it was a sin

00:19:10.518 --> 00:19:13.754
for a man to divorce his wife, even if she had murdered her parents,

00:19:13.792 --> 00:19:16.382
His sister and some movie projectionist that she'd slept with.

00:19:16.436 --> 00:19:19.114
Hopefully, for Howard's sake, she spared him those last details.

00:19:19.162 --> 00:19:22.666
Or maybe he stayed with her out of fear of becoming her next target or even

00:19:22.708 --> 00:19:24.594
being blamed for the murders.

00:19:24.632 --> 00:19:27.954
Later on Pearl reflects on this time, which may offer a

00:19:27.992 --> 00:19:29.134
much simpler reason for Howard's compliance.

00:19:29.262 --> 00:19:31.934
-[Pearl] There wasn't anything you wouldn't do for me back then.

00:19:31.982 --> 00:19:34.638
-[Pearl] That's the power of beauty.

00:19:34.734 --> 00:19:36.770
♪ I did it all for the Nookie! ♪

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:41.302
Anyway, the flu pandemic came to an end, then the Roaring 20s happened,

00:19:41.356 --> 00:19:42.642
followed by the Great Depression.

00:19:42.706 --> 00:19:45.974
Pearl never mentions children, and we know that she hated being pregnant, so

00:19:46.012 --> 00:19:48.326
there's no reason to believe that she and Howard would have started a family.

00:19:48.348 --> 00:19:51.634
We know that Pearl was left alone on the farm yet again when Howard

00:19:51.682 --> 00:19:53.942
volunteered to fight in World War II.

00:19:54.006 --> 00:19:57.450
By the time he came home from that war, pearl was almost 50 years old.

00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:00.458
We don't know exactly what happened in the 30 years after the war, but we

00:20:00.464 --> 00:20:03.062
know that Pearl succeeded in saving what she had with Howard.

00:20:03.126 --> 00:20:06.046
Either way, the easiest assumption is that Pearl remained on the farm with

00:20:06.068 --> 00:20:08.670
Howard until we see her again in 1979.

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:11.786
Pearl couldn't hide her dark side from Howard, so maybe Howard protected

00:20:11.818 --> 00:20:14.638
Pearl like her mother did by keeping her isolated on the farm, where the

00:20:14.644 --> 00:20:16.158
world wouldn't see her dark side.

00:20:16.244 --> 00:20:19.746
However, it would be safe to assume that Mitsy was not her last victim in

00:20:19.768 --> 00:20:23.266
the younger half of her life, because 60 years is a long time not to run

00:20:23.288 --> 00:20:25.934
into a missionary or a Girl Scout or a census taker.

00:20:25.982 --> 00:20:29.154
And Howard still seems to want to shelter her, even in their elder years.

00:20:29.272 --> 00:20:32.226
At some point, Howard came down with a heart condition and eventually grew

00:20:32.258 --> 00:20:33.462
too old to do farm work.

00:20:33.516 --> 00:20:37.062
So in the 1970s, they started renting out a guest house for a little extra income.

00:20:37.116 --> 00:20:41.174
Howard confesses to Jackson Hole that a Bohemian renter died for

00:20:41.212 --> 00:20:42.502
trying to entice Pearl.

00:20:42.566 --> 00:20:46.346
Was the other renter actually trying to entice Pearl? Probably not, but we

00:20:46.368 --> 00:20:49.754
see this poor Bohemian hanging naked from the basement ceiling later on, so

00:20:49.792 --> 00:20:51.622
we do know that he was probably murdered.

00:20:51.686 --> 00:20:55.322
Did Pearl kill him for rejecting her? Did Howard kill him out of jealousy?

00:20:55.386 --> 00:20:58.494
Whatever it was, there's a messed up dynamic happening on this farm, and

00:20:58.532 --> 00:21:01.594
things get messed up when a film crew from Houston rents out the guest house.

00:21:01.642 --> 00:21:04.606
Howard likely would have never let them stay if they knew that they

00:21:04.628 --> 00:21:06.166
were there to shoot an adult's film,

00:21:06.218 --> 00:21:09.618
Considering Pearl's history of delusions of stardom, pearl watches as the

00:21:09.624 --> 00:21:10.402
crew pulls up.

00:21:10.456 --> 00:21:13.138
Their leader, Wayne, even does the shaven haircut thing when he knocks on

00:21:13.144 --> 00:21:14.130
their front door.

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:19.734
Little does he know Pearl and Howard are both over 80 years old.

00:21:19.772 --> 00:21:22.722
At this point, they can remember when things actually cost two bits.

00:21:22.786 --> 00:21:26.726
Pearl seems fixated as she stares longingly at Maxine, the young star of the

00:21:26.748 --> 00:21:28.578
adult movie, through an upstairs window.

00:21:28.674 --> 00:21:31.786
This could be because Maxine looks a lot like Pearl did when she was younger.

00:21:31.808 --> 00:21:33.894
In fact, they look exactly alike.

00:21:33.942 --> 00:21:36.422
Because Mia Goth plays both Pearl and Maxine.

00:21:36.486 --> 00:21:37.654
It's not a subtle choice.

00:21:37.702 --> 00:21:39.226
It's history repeating itself.

00:21:39.328 --> 00:21:42.086
Both young women are consumed with their obsession to become famous starlets.

00:21:42.118 --> 00:21:44.454
Pearl and Howard seem to have an arrangement.

00:21:44.502 --> 00:21:46.890
Howard talks to the renters and Pearl keeps to herself.

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.750
Religion remains a big part of their lives.

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:52.014
Their TV is constantly tuned into a channel featuring sermons from a fire

00:21:52.052 --> 00:21:55.134
and brimstone preacher who warns of sex fiends lurking where they least

00:21:55.172 --> 00:21:55.870
expect it.

00:21:55.940 --> 00:21:59.506
So when Howard finally meets this group of young, underdressed guests, he

00:21:59.528 --> 00:22:02.514
doesn't like it, especially because he knows that it might set Pearl off.

00:22:02.552 --> 00:22:04.578
So he warns the crew to stay away from her.

00:22:04.664 --> 00:22:09.422
-[Howard] My wife is next door, so I would appreciate a little discretion.

00:22:09.566 --> 00:22:12.518
They assumed he was just being old fashioned and protecting his wife from

00:22:12.524 --> 00:22:13.314
the indecency.

00:22:13.362 --> 00:22:16.262
But what they don't understand is that Howard is actually protecting them

00:22:16.316 --> 00:22:17.122
from his wife.

00:22:17.186 --> 00:22:20.706
But Pearl's curiosity is too strong and she spies on her much younger

00:22:20.738 --> 00:22:24.166
doppelgänger skinny dipping in Theta's old swamp where a new gator,

00:22:24.198 --> 00:22:26.310
possibly Theda's grandchild, has taken up residence.

00:22:26.390 --> 00:22:29.386
It's unclear whether Pearl is interested in Maxine's beauty or the

00:22:29.408 --> 00:22:32.566
possibility of seeing her torn apart by the alligator, but I'm guessing it's both.

00:22:32.598 --> 00:22:35.982
Maxine unknowingly escapes and Pearl continues to follow her.

00:22:36.036 --> 00:22:39.034
Eventually, they see each other and Pearl waves sheepishly from the porch.

00:22:39.082 --> 00:22:41.434
Maxine wanders into the house and does a little snooping.

00:22:41.482 --> 00:22:44.674
If Pearl ever was the happy homemaker she said she wanted to be, she's not anymore.

00:22:44.712 --> 00:22:46.178
The place is a mess.

00:22:46.264 --> 00:22:49.422
Pearl doesn't seem to mind Maxine snooping because she offers her a beverage

00:22:49.486 --> 00:22:51.220
in the creepiest way possible.

00:22:51.917 --> 00:22:53.917
– [PEARL] Lemonade?

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:57.474
Maxine accepts the offer and the two sit at the table and share a wonderful

00:22:57.522 --> 00:22:58.470
conversation.

00:22:58.470 --> 00:23:05.406
(Pearl and Maxine sit in silence)

00:23:05.690 --> 00:23:08.816
Okay, it's not so much a conversation as much as it is

00:23:08.816 --> 00:23:11.217
Pearl staring at Maxine in deafening silence.

00:23:11.217 --> 00:23:15.398
Understandably creeped out, She chugs her lemonade and does something we know that Pearl can't stand

00:23:15.484 --> 00:23:17.018
makes up an excuse to leave.

00:23:17.104 --> 00:23:20.486
Pearl walks her to the door, but not before taking a trip down memory lane

00:23:20.518 --> 00:23:22.810
as she sees herself in Maxine's face.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:24.780
-[Pearl] Such a special face. 

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:32.114
-[Pearl] Beautiful. 

00:23:32.114 --> 00:23:33.866
Howard arrives home and breaks up the party.

00:23:33.898 --> 00:23:36.730
So Pearl tells Maxine to leave and keep their encounter a secret.

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:39.774
She knows she's not supposed to be interacting with the guests.

00:23:39.812 --> 00:23:41.038
Just like after seeing the pretty girls in the movies, 

00:23:41.044 --> 00:23:44.386
so many years ago, Pearl once again attempts to recapture her

00:23:44.408 --> 00:23:47.150
youthful beauty by combing her hair and putting on makeup.

00:23:47.230 --> 00:23:49.906
At some point, although this doesn't happen on screen, Pearl must have

00:23:49.928 --> 00:23:53.154
communicated to Howard that she wanted Maxine, who they later refer to as

00:23:53.192 --> 00:23:55.582
the One, and this most likely happened that afternoon.

00:23:55.646 --> 00:23:58.854
When they discuss this later on, however, he still isn't clear on which girl

00:23:58.892 --> 00:24:02.066
Pearl has her eye on, and it's not clear if he wanted her to start killing

00:24:02.098 --> 00:24:03.830
or if he was actually trying to prevent it.

00:24:03.900 --> 00:24:07.426
Luckily, this isn't an analysis of Howard, but it's worth noting.

00:24:07.468 --> 00:24:10.486
That evening, she sneaks out and attempts to live vicariously as she watches

00:24:10.518 --> 00:24:14.394
Maxine film her scene through the cabin window, just as her delusions about

00:24:14.432 --> 00:24:18.426
her own self image ran wild in 1918, she sees these relations happen and

00:24:18.448 --> 00:24:20.282
believes that she can have the same effect.

00:24:20.416 --> 00:24:23.678
That evening, she dresses up and tries to seduce Howard, which he has to

00:24:23.684 --> 00:24:25.198
turn down because of his bad heart.

00:24:25.284 --> 00:24:28.762
Once again, Pearl can't get what she wants, while those younger and prettier

00:24:28.826 --> 00:24:30.270
get everything that she's ever wanted.

00:24:30.340 --> 00:24:32.190
It's the dance tryout all over again.

00:24:32.260 --> 00:24:35.822
Later that night, she wakes up unable to contain her geriatric horniness,

00:24:35.886 --> 00:24:37.774
and ends up scaring the crap out of the heartbroken

00:24:37.822 --> 00:24:39.502
Camera guy on his way out of the farm.

00:24:39.566 --> 00:24:42.194
He gets out of the van to check on her as if she were a loose patient

00:24:42.242 --> 00:24:43.878
wandering the halls of a nursing home.

00:24:43.964 --> 00:24:47.548
Also, everyone's favorite song, which is totally not overused in movies and TV

00:24:47.548 --> 00:24:49.248
is playing on the radio.

00:24:49.248 --> 00:24:52.296
♪ Don't Fear the Reaper ♪

00:24:52.570 --> 00:24:55.938
Little does he know, Pearl is the same desperate, attention starved woman

00:24:55.954 --> 00:24:56.874
that she's always been.

00:24:56.912 --> 00:24:59.178
And when he goes to help, she tries to kiss him.

00:24:59.264 --> 00:25:01.580
-[Pearl] Look at me like you looked at her.

00:25:02.110 --> 00:25:06.010
-[RJ] What? 
-[Pearl] I can show you what I'm capable of.

00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:09.526
The camera guy politely declines, and Pearl, predictably, does not handle

00:25:09.558 --> 00:25:10.410
the rejection well.

00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:13.774
She stabs him in the neck, 23 times, to be exact, I guess kind of making

00:25:13.812 --> 00:25:16.190
good on her promise of showing him what she's capable of.

00:25:16.260 --> 00:25:19.166
After the murder, Pearl takes a moment to dance in her own little dream world,

00:25:19.198 --> 00:25:22.338
just like she was doing when we first met her, and also like the

00:25:22.344 --> 00:25:23.234
first time we met her.

00:25:23.272 --> 00:25:26.530
She is unable to stop after just one victim.

00:25:26.530 --> 00:25:29.597
(Impact)

00:25:31.316 --> 00:25:34.747
♪ Stinger ♪

00:25:35.290 --> 00:25:38.114
As Howard searches the grounds for her, Pearl stalks Wayne.

00:25:38.162 --> 00:25:41.106
As he searches the barn for his missing cameraman, he notices Pearl's

00:25:41.138 --> 00:25:43.766
movement around the barn's perimeter, leading him to peek through a hole in

00:25:43.788 --> 00:25:44.092
the wall.

00:25:44.092 --> 00:25:47.258
And when he does, Pearl stabs him in the eye with her weapon of choice a pitchfork.

00:25:47.264 --> 00:25:50.886
Later, Pearl walks into the barn, casting a devilish silhouette

00:25:50.918 --> 00:25:53.142
to finish the job with a pretty weak pitchfork stab.

00:25:53.206 --> 00:25:55.386
Not bad for an octogenarian, I guess.

00:25:55.488 --> 00:25:58.586
From there, she makes her way into Maxine's bedroom and climbs into bed with

00:25:58.608 --> 00:26:02.202
her for a little skin to skin spooning sesh with strawberry syrup.

00:26:02.266 --> 00:26:05.486
Eventually, maxine wakes up, realizes that this is not her boyfriend, and

00:26:05.508 --> 00:26:08.954
runs out of the room, startling Bobby-Lynne, the blonde co-star of the adult film.

00:26:09.002 --> 00:26:12.206
As Pearl heads down to the pier, Bobby-Lynne follows her, fearing that

00:26:12.228 --> 00:26:13.950
the old woman might be having an episode.

00:26:14.030 --> 00:26:16.926
Who would have thought that these dirty film types would be so solicitous

00:26:16.958 --> 00:26:20.226
about the welfare of a crazy old woman? Pearl slaps BBobby-Lynne for her

00:26:20.248 --> 00:26:23.138
trouble, letting her old jealous tendencies dictate her behavior.

00:26:23.234 --> 00:26:27.046
-[Pearl] Why should you get to have it all? What have you ever done except be a whore?

00:26:27.068 --> 00:26:30.386
Pearl shoves Bobby-Lynne into the swamp, where she quickly becomes gator food.

00:26:30.418 --> 00:26:32.594
So much for being a good Samaritan.

00:26:32.642 --> 00:26:34.194
Pearl finally meets up with Howard. He asks her if that was the one.

00:26:34.242 --> 00:26:38.046
-[Pearl] You know I don't like blondes. 

00:26:38.178 --> 00:26:41.126
Guess she still hasn't forgotten about being snubbed from the church dance

00:26:41.158 --> 00:26:42.710
group 61 years prior.

00:26:42.790 --> 00:26:45.494
They continue looking for Maxine in the room where she was sleeping.

00:26:45.542 --> 00:26:48.618
Howard tells Pearl that he's got the sound girl Lorraine trapped in the basement.

00:26:48.624 --> 00:26:51.450
But Pearl is disappointed because she wants Maxine.

00:26:51.530 --> 00:26:53.946
She sees her as special because of their similarities.

00:26:54.058 --> 00:26:55.998
Pearl asks him to tell her that she's special.

00:26:56.084 --> 00:26:59.278
Although they've spent many decades together, she still feels the need to be

00:26:59.284 --> 00:27:00.762
told that she's loved and admired after all of these years.

00:27:00.826 --> 00:27:03.730
She's like the world's oldest pick-me-girl.

00:27:03.800 --> 00:27:07.394
So Howard makes love to Pearl, heart be damned, and not realizing that

00:27:07.432 --> 00:27:11.538
Maxine is listening to all of this from under the bed, scarred for life.

00:27:11.624 --> 00:27:15.538
We can't be sure if Pearl or Howard successfully finished the job, and I

00:27:15.544 --> 00:27:16.254
don't want to know.

00:27:16.312 --> 00:27:19.078
But we do know that they eventually followed the fleeing Maxine back to

00:27:19.084 --> 00:27:21.398
their main house, where she was attempting to free Lorraine from the basement.

00:27:21.404 --> 00:27:24.306
Lorraine tries to make her escape out the front door, but Pearl

00:27:24.338 --> 00:27:25.382
and Howard are ready for her.

00:27:25.436 --> 00:27:28.106
Howard blasts her with a shotgun right there on the front porch and

00:27:28.128 --> 00:27:29.850
immediately begins planning the cover up.

00:27:29.920 --> 00:27:34.346
-[Howard] If nobody shows up by tomorrow, we'll take the body and we'll dump her in

00:27:34.368 --> 00:27:35.674
-[Howard] the pond with the others.

00:27:35.792 --> 00:27:38.794
Pearl watches as Howard moves Lorraine's body back inside the house.

00:27:38.832 --> 00:27:42.078
But when Lorraine twitches ever so slightly, it scares him so badly that he

00:27:42.084 --> 00:27:42.878
has a heart attack.

00:27:42.964 --> 00:27:45.422
Pearl runs to his aid, begging Maxine for help.

00:27:45.476 --> 00:27:49.170
But Maxine responds by pulling a gun on her, which, as we've come to expect,

00:27:49.240 --> 00:27:52.066
sends her adoration towards the younger girl, all the way to the other end

00:27:52.088 --> 00:27:54.414
of the spectrum into blind fury.

00:27:54.542 --> 00:27:55.504
-[Pearl] Deviant little whore.

00:27:57.499 --> 00:27:58.351
-[Pearl] Poor thing.

00:28:00.918 --> 00:28:02.550
-[Pearl]  You’ll end up just like me.

00:28:02.550 --> 00:28:04.962
At this moment, Pearl truly sounds like her mother.

00:28:05.026 --> 00:28:09.010
And worse yet, Maxine looks and sounds exactly like Pearl did in her youth.

00:28:09.090 --> 00:28:10.550
-[Maxine] I'm a star.

00:28:10.700 --> 00:28:12.774
-[Maxine] The whole world is gonna know my name.

00:28:12.892 --> 00:28:16.306
Unfortunately for Maxine, she was not counting on her gun being empty.

00:28:16.338 --> 00:28:19.242
And this gives Pearl the chance to pick up the shotgun and fire back against her.

00:28:19.296 --> 00:28:22.186
The blast sends Pearl flying backwards through the screen door and

00:28:22.208 --> 00:28:23.382
causes her to break her hip.

00:28:23.446 --> 00:28:25.002
All she can do is beg for help.

00:28:25.056 --> 00:28:28.874
As Maxine brushes past and leaves her for dead, Pearl's dying words reflect

00:28:28.922 --> 00:28:32.650
a life of regret, of prayers unanswered and dreams unfulfilled.

00:28:32.730 --> 00:28:34.110
-[Pearl] You're not innocent.

00:28:36.530 --> 00:28:38.000
-[Pearl] You're not special.

00:28:39.650 --> 00:28:45.402
-[Pearl] It'll all be taken from you, just like it was from me.

00:28:45.556 --> 00:28:48.450
Even in her dying moments, Pearl didn't get what she wanted.

00:28:48.520 --> 00:28:49.694
She wanted to be loved.

00:28:49.742 --> 00:28:52.606
She wanted to be a star, to be seen and be appreciated.

00:28:52.718 --> 00:28:56.298
Instead, she frightened people and at the end she was physically repulsive

00:28:56.334 --> 00:28:58.950
to the crowd she so desperately wanted to be a part of.

00:28:59.020 --> 00:29:01.814
While we have no way of knowing exactly what happened on the farm between

00:29:01.852 --> 00:29:06.086
World War I and 1979, we do know that at least one unlucky Bohemian was

00:29:06.108 --> 00:29:06.982
murdered in that time.

00:29:07.036 --> 00:29:10.506
And Howard was very aware of what might happen if Pearl got to interact with

00:29:10.528 --> 00:29:11.590
the adults film crew.

00:29:11.670 --> 00:29:15.002
Someone as mentally disturbed as Pearl doesn't just get better over time

00:29:15.056 --> 00:29:15.958
without treatment.

00:29:16.054 --> 00:29:18.982
One thing we do know is that Pearl's life was ultimately a tragedy.

00:29:19.046 --> 00:29:21.998
In her final moments, before her skull got flattened under the tires of a

00:29:22.004 --> 00:29:24.670
truck she watched Maxine prepare to leave the farm for good.

00:29:24.740 --> 00:29:27.966
Pearl yearned to leave so desperately in her youth, but she never got the chance.

00:29:27.988 --> 00:29:30.830
Both Pearl and X were made by A24.

